// A borrowed reference to a generic instantiation. Marked xfail: '&Box[i64]'
// does not parse as a type.
//
// A bare instantiation is a perfectly good type -- generic-success declares a
// variable of one and passes one by value -- but the type parser will not take
// one after '&'. It reports ErrorNotTyped twice, "Expected a typed expression"
// at the instantiation and "Expected a type" at the reference.
//
// The consequence reaches past this group. It is why 'union' matches Option
// and Result by value rather than by reference, and it will block any generic
// collection whose methods take '&self'.
//
// When this scenario starts passing, drop the xfail and fold it into
// generic-success as a printed fact.

struct Box[T] {
  v T
}

fn peek(b &Box[i64]) i64 {
  b.v
}
